-- title:
--   Properness of the two-chart integral model over a Noetherian base
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ an element with $j \neq 0$. For a subset $S \subseteq F$ write $\mathrm{chartAlg}\,R\,F\,S$ for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those $x \in F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ generated by $S$; thus `chartAlgFin R F j` is the integral closure of $R[j]$ in $F$ and `chartAlgInf R F j` is the integral closure of $R[j^{-1}]$ in $F$. Assume both of these subalgebras are $R$-algebras of finite type. The scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout, in the category of schemes, of the two morphisms $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the algebra inclusions `inclFin` and `inclInf` of `chartAlgFin R F j` and `chartAlgInf R F j` into the overlap algebra, i.e. of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the overlap ring mapping to $\mathrm{Spec}$ of each of the two chart rings; and `toBase R F j` is the morphism from this pushout to $\mathrm{Spec}\,R$ obtained from the two structure morphisms $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin}) \to \mathrm{Spec}\,R$ and $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgInf}) \to \mathrm{Spec}\,R$, which agree on the overlap. The assertion is that `toBase R F j` is a proper morphism of schemes.
--
--   This is the properness of the integral two-chart model of a curve glued from the integral closures of $R[j]$ and $R[j^{-1}]$ in a field $F$, established over an arbitrary Noetherian base under the finiteness assumption on the two charts. It is used in the construction of normal proper models of function fields over valuation-theoretic bases, and in particular for the models of modular curves built from a Hauptmodul $j$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_isProper_toBase.lean

